				<element type="warning_sequence">2</element>
                <text type="warning_situation">
				<p>MINOR FLOODING POSSIBLE ALONG BREMER RIVER AND WARRILL CREEK WITH STORMS FROM OVERNIGHT TUESDAY INTO WEDNESDAY</p>

				<p/>
				<p>Rainfall totals up to approximately 20 mm have been recorded across the Bremer and Warrill catchments since late Tuesday afternoon. Further showers and thunderstorms are possible during Tuesday evening and into early Wednesday. Heavy rain remains possible in parts of the catchments with thunderstorm activity, though the timing and location of heavy falls remain uncertain. </p>
<p/>
<p>Catchments are relatively wet and are likely to respond quickly to rainfall. Depending on the timing and location of the heaviest falls, minor flooding may develop along the Bremer River and Warrill Creek from overnight Tuesday into Wednesday. Higher levels may be possible. The situation is being closely monitored and this warning will be updated as required.</p>

				<p/>

                </text>
                <element type="severity">Minor</element>
            </forecast-period>
